$$\tab\tab\tab    Since the entire macro string ends with two successive <ESC>\par
\tab\tab\tab    characters, this ends the macro input as TECO is initialized.\par
                     Macro execution starts with the first character of the file.\page\tab\tab\tab    Note: The exact process of macro initialization is extremely\par
\tab\tab\tab    version-dependent.  As such, it is good practice to avoid the\par
                     use of the textual Q-registers X, Y and Z; certain TECO\par
\tab\tab\tab    implementations (other than TECOC) pass macro string arguments\par
